    "definition": "Var(X)=E[(X-E[X])²]; Var(aX+b)=a²Var(X); Cov(U,V)=E[(U-E[U])(V-E[V])].",
    "assumptions": [
      "All probabilities are nonnegative and normalized.",
      "Finite support/finite second moments.",
      "Physical units are mV for errors and mV² for second moments.",
      "Zero covariance does not generally imply independence."
    ],
